module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.realization_violates_its_declared_complexity_contract

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import std.decl_ref { DeclarationRef, WholeDeclaration }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data realization_violates_its_declared_complexity_contract: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "realization_violates_its_declared_complexity_contract" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a primitive's realization costs more than its declared complexity contract, and every algorithm built on the contract inherits the difference silently** INVALID STATE: `std.primitives` `concat_contract` declares concat at log(n + m) on the persistent carrier, and the comment beside the `rc_*` ops in `v1.compiler.runtime_rust` `rt_rc_container_ops` states the same for every update. Yet `rc_list_concat` realized concat as `Rc::make_mut(&mut a).extend(b.iter().cloned())`, one push_back per element of `b`, so a concat cost the length of its right operand. The interpreter's free `concat` arm had the same shape, worse: it copied BOTH operands into a fresh vector.",

    "HARM: a .dag author reasoning correctly from the declared contract writes an algorithm that is linear under it and quadratic under the realization, and nothing reports the gap. SPECIMEN: `v2.std.node` `node_subtree_nodes` is a bottom-up fold whose step is `concat(acc, sub)` -- O(n log n) under the contract, O(n * depth) as realized -- and `v2.compiler.normalize` `normalize_with` calls it on every parse tree. A comma list parses as a right-nested repeat chain about N deep, so normalize of `extdeps.cpu.ampere_altra_package_table4_raw` (one 4,926-row list literal) took 161 s on the emitted compiler, and the v2 native census of the whole tree ran for hours and read as a hang (runs 37348196148 and 37197235156).",

    "HOW IT WAS FOUND, AND WHY THE INTERPRETER HID IT. Eval steps on the interpreter were LINEAR in list size with the call memo off (Int list 400 to 800: x2.00) while CPU per step grew -- the cost lived inside one counted step, which is exactly what a step budget cannot see. Only perf on the emitted binary named it: 96.6% inclusive under `node_subtree_nodes`, 82% under `rc_list_concat`, self time in im chunk make_mut, drop_slow and Rrb push_back. A READING of the carrier had also cleared it: `gunbc.build_target` `aggregate_findings` carried an annotation that checked `rc_list_concat` against both realizations and concluded the spine was shared -- true of the clone, false of the extend that followed it. The contract was stated twice and executed by nothing.",

    "DISTINCT FROM `primitive_operation_carries_two_cost_authorities`, which is two DECLARATIONS of one operation's cost that disagree. Here the declarations agree and the REALIZATION disagrees with both; deciding which declaration wins would not have found it. Distinct from `memo_key_cost_proportional_to_argument_size`, where the cost is in a memo's key, not in the primitive.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- found by a profiler after the harm, with no gate. ATTAINABLE CEILING: mechanically preventable, NOT structural. The complexity of a host realization is a property of target code the .dag cannot represent, so no accepted .dag program can be made to exclude it; what can be enforced is a scaling control per declared contract, run on the realization that ships.",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, naming the capability: a scaling control enrolled per `PrimitiveContract` with a declared persistent cost, executed on the EMITTED realization (not the interpreter, whose step counter cannot see work inside a step) at two sizes, refusing when the measured ratio exceeds the contract's -- sufficient that a realization of any contracted primitive that walks an operand reds before a consumer is built on it. Explicitly NOT discharged by: an annotation reading the carrier; an eval-step budget; or repairing concat alone, since the population is every contracted primitive.",

    "UNCERTAINTY CARRIED: the audit of the list ops in `rt_rc_container_ops` and the bare-Vec prelude (push, snoc, concat, list_concat) found the extend shape only in concat and list_concat, both repaired; map and set merges iterate their overlay and are outside the list contract audited here. The other contracted primitives have NOT been measured.",
  ],

  evidence: [
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "std.primitives", decl_name: "concat_contract", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.std.node", decl_name: "node_subtree_nodes", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "v2.compiler.normalize", decl_name: "normalize_with", field: WholeDeclaration },
    DeclarationRef { module_path: "gunbc.build_target", decl_name: "aggregate_findings", field: WholeDeclaration },
  ],
}
